<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaliman Asen I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1234–1246</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Koloman I of Bulgaria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaliman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-asen-i">Asen I</a> was tsar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> from 1241 to 1246, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-asen-ii">Ivan Asen II</a> as a boy of about seven. His regents paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> after their raids of 1242 and could not stop losses to the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a>. He died young in 1246, possibly poisoned.</p></div>
